ዓለም።", "language": "Geez", "validation": "unapplied_whole_printed_unit_candidate", "chapter_file": "sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch68.txt + sources/enoch/ethiopic/transcribed/charles_1906/ch69.txt", "pages": [159, 160]}, "current_canonical_source_text": "በእንተ'ዝ፡ ይመጽእ፡ ላዕሌሆሙ፡ ኵሉ፡ ዘኅቡእ፡ ለዓለመ፡", "translation": {"text": "Because of this[b][a], everything hidden forever shall come upon them.", "philosophy": "optimal-equivalence", "footnotes": [{"marker": "a", "text": "Or 'all that has been concealed for the age' or 'everything hidden from of old.' The final term can carry the sense of eternity, an age, or ancient duration.", "reason": "lexical_alternative"}, {"marker": "b", "text": "Or 'everything hidden forever shall come upon them.'.", "reason": "previous_rendering"}]}}]
