{
  "chapter_complete": false,
  "reviews": [
    {
      "reference": "1 Enoch 68:1",
      "verdict": "hold",
      "reason": "The English promotes 'my grandfather Hēnok' to the explicit subject of 'gave me', although the printed grandfather expression is introduced by እም- after 'in a book'. That syntactic relationship must remain visible rather than being silently rearranged. Neither 'from the words of Hēnok' nor the supplied exact grandfather glyph sequence is sufficiently secure for approval here. The plural ወይመርሙ also requires an unresolved 'they', not an automatically supplied grandfather subject. Preserve both printed asterisks.",
      "suggested_text": "",
      "footnote_changes": "Remove the unsupported 'from the words of Hēnok' alternative. Explain the book/from-grandfather construction and the unresolved subject of the final plural verb. Attach the similitudes alternative directly to 'parables'; remove the obsolete previous-rendering note.",
      "suggested_source_text": ""
    },
    {
      "reference": "1 Enoch 68:2",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "reason": "Michael speaks to Raphael; the names must not be reversed. The printed wording contains two occurrences of ለእዝኒ, 'for the ear', both suppressed by the current English. 'Severity of the judgment concerning the hidden secrets' therefore smooths away substantive source wording. The judgment word near the end reads ኵነኔ, not the supplied ጽነኒ. The final plural verb does not name bodily organs as its subject.",
      "suggested_text": "And on that day Michael answered, saying to Raphael, “The power of the spirit seizes me and agitates me because of the terrible thing for the ear, concerning hidden things for the ear. Who is there who can endure the terrible thing, since judgment has been carried out and they melt away before it?”",
      "footnote_changes": "Place a textual-difficulty note at the repeated ear-language, explicitly preserving both occurrences. Note that the subject of 'they melt away' is unstated; do not identify it as hearts or kidneys. Remove or relocate 'drives me on', which is presently attached to the wrong clause. Do not present judgment as merely the severity of a revelation.",
      "suggested_source_text": "ወ*ይእቲ፡ ዕለት፡ አውሥአ፡ ሚካኤል፡ እንዘ፡ ይብል፡ ለሩፋኤል፡ ኀይሉ፡ ለመንፈስ፡ *ይመሥጠኒ፡ ወያምዕዐኒ፡ በእንተ፡ ዕፁቡ፡ ለእዝኒ፡ እንተ፡ ኅቡኣት፡ ለእዝኒ፡ መኑ፡ ውእቱ፡ ዘይክል፡ ተዐግሦተ፡ ዕፁበ፡ በእንተ፡ ተገብረት፡ ኵነኔ፡ ወይትመሰዉ፡ በቅድሜሃ።"
    },
    {
      "reference": "1 Enoch 68:3",
      "verdict": "hold",
      "reason": "The printed judgment expression is ቃለ፡ *ኵነኔ፡, 'word of judgment', not 'word of severity' followed by an additional sentence noun. Preserve [እምኔሆሙ፡] as bracketed printed material. The current 'because of those who brought them out' supplies a causal relationship and resolves the difficult attachment without warrant. The heart and kidneys express inward response; the verse does not depict those organs literally melting.",
      "suggested_text": "",
      "footnote_changes": "Move the kidneys/inward-parts note from Raphael to 'kidneys'. Identify the bracketed expression explicitly as 'from them' and leave its attachment and the identities of the plural pronouns unresolved. Remove 'from before them?' as an alternative to the heart clause. Do not omit Michael or adopt a Greek/conjectural reconstruction without identifying its separate evidential basis.",
      "suggested_source_text": "ወአውሥአ፡ ካዕበ፡ ወይቤሎ፡ ሚካኤል፡ ለሩፋኤል፡ መኑ፡ ውእቱ፡ ዘኢይረክሕ፡ ልቡ፡ ዲቤሃ፡ ወኢይትሀወክ፡ ኵልያቲሁ፡ እምዛቲ፡ ቃለ፡ *ኵነኔ፡ ወፅእት፡ ዲቤሆሙ፡ [እምኔሆሙ፡] ዘአውፅእዎሙ፡ ከመዝ።"
    },
    {
      "reference": "1 Enoch 68:4",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "reason": "ወኢይከውን፡ ሎሙ does not explicitly name the subject of the negative clause. Capitalized 'He' encourages identification with God or another person that the printed wording does not establish. The advocacy/support explanation is interpretation, not an expressed source noun. The final clause should not silently become a statement about plural 'lords'.",
      "suggested_text": "And it happened, when he stood before the Lord of Spirits, that Michael spoke thus to Raphael: “And it will not be for them in the sight of the Lord, for the Lord of Spirits is angry with them, because they act like the Lord.”",
      "footnote_changes": "Attach a note directly to 'it will not be for them': 'The subject is not expressed, and what will not be for them remains unclear.' Remove the advocacy explanation as the presumed meaning, the redundant previous-rendering note, and the unsupported plural-lords alternative.",
      "suggested_source_text": "ወኮነ፡ ሶበ፡ ቆመ፡ በቅድመ፡ እግዚአ፡ መናፍስት፡ ወከመዝ፡ ይቤሎ፡ ሚካኤል፡ ለሩፋኤል፡ ወኢይከውን፡ ሎሙ፡ በውስተ፡ ዓይነ፡ እግዚአ፡ እስመ፡ እግዚአ፡ መናፍስት፡ ተምዕዖሙ፡ እስመ፡ እምሳለ፡ እግዚአ፡ ይገብሩ።"
    },
    {
      "reference": "1 Enoch 68:5",
      "verdict": "hold",
      "reason": "The canonical source and English stop mid-unit at the bottom of p121. The verse continues on p122 through the second ለዓለመ፡ ዓለም። immediately before LXIX. The candidate also miscopies the printed negative prefixes: ኢመላእክ, ወኢብእሲ, and ኢ*ይትፄመው, not forms beginning with እ. The continuation includes sharing, a portion, 'they alone', receiving, and their judgment; none is represented in the canonical English. The relationships among 'them', the sharers, and 'they alone' must not be resolved merely for fluency.",
